## Why This Is Asked

This evaluates the ability to design a plugin-friendly, runtime-extensible load balancing system for edge proxies, focusing on decoupling and safe dynamic strategy selection.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern for algorithm abstraction
- Registry-based plugin architecture
- Runtime extensibility without core modifications
- State management for routing decisions
- Isolated testing of individual strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
interface LoadBalancingStrategy {
  selectPeer(route: any, peers: string[], state: any): string;
}

class Registry {
  private map = new Map<string, LoadBalancingStrategy>();

  register(name: string, strategy: LoadBalancingStrategy) {
    this.map.set(name, strategy);
  }

  get(name: string): LoadBalancingStrategy {
    return this.map.get(name);
  }
}

// Example usage
class RoundRobinStrategy implements LoadBalancingStrategy {
  selectPeer(route: any, peers: string[], state: any): string {
    const index = state[route.id] || 0;
    state[route.id] = (index + 1) % peers.length;
    return peers[index];
  }
}

const registry = new Registry();
registry.register('round_robin', new RoundRobinStrategy());
```

